&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by more than 45 million+ developers and 500,000 organizations, including 98% of the Fortune 500. Postman is helping developers and professionals across the globe build the API-first world by simplifying each step of the API lifecycle and streamlining collaboration—enabling users to create better APIs, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in San Francisco and has offices in Boston, New York, Austin, Tokyo, London, and Bangalore - where Postman was founded. Postman is privately held, with funding from Battery Ventures, BOND, Coatue, CRV, Insight Partners, and Nexus Venture Partners. Learn more at postman.com or connect with Postman on X via @getpostman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Fern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fern is building the enterprise agent layer for APIs and is backed by Postman, giving us access to a platform used by more than 40 million developers and 98% of the Fortune 500. We operate with the focus, speed, and ownership of a startup while benefiting from Postman’s enterprise reach, distribution, and API ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As AI agents increasingly become the primary consumers of APIs, companies need more than traditional developer documentation. Agents require structured context, strongly typed interfaces, deterministic contracts, and reliable tools for discovering and executing API functionality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fern helps enterprises make their APIs accessible to both developers and agents through four connected product surfaces:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation&lt;/strong&gt; that organizes technical knowledge into structured, agent-readable context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SDKs&lt;/strong&gt; that provide strongly typed, production-ready interfaces across major programming languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLI tooling&lt;/strong&gt; that allows developers and agents to interact with APIs directly from their workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MCP servers&lt;/strong&gt; that give AI agents a standardized way to discover and use API capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive (Corporate/Enterprise), you will partner directly with engineering and platform leaders to modernize how their APIs are consumed by developers and AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run consultative, technically rigorous enterprise sales cycles that guide customers through hands-on evaluations of Fern’s documentation, SDK, CLI, and MCP products. You will help prospects understand how Fern can improve developer experience, establish API governance, and create an agent-ready interface for their platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the full sales cycle. &lt;/strong&gt;You will source opportunities, run discovery, coordinate technical validation, navigate procurement, and close business. You will partner closely with Sales Engineering to build tailored demonstrations and guide customers through detailed product evaluations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sell to technical and executive stakeholders. &lt;/strong&gt;Your buyers will include VPs of Engineering, Platform and Infrastructure leaders, Staff Engineers, Developer Experience teams, and technical executives. You will need the curiosity and credibility to discuss API architecture, SDK quality, CI/CD workflows, documentation systems, MCP, and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive consultative enterprise deals. &lt;/strong&gt;Fern is not a transactional product sale. Customers are often evaluating Fern as a strategic layer between their APIs, developers, and AI agents. You will help organizations quantify the operational and commercial impact of improving API adoption, reducing integration friction, and making their platform agent-ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigate complex organizations. &lt;/strong&gt;You will build alignment across engineering, product, security, procurement, and executive leadership. Successful deals require strong multi-threading, clear business cases, and disciplined control of the evaluation process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can be considered for Corporate if you have 2+ years of B2B SaaS sales closing experience in Developer/IT/Security technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can be considered for Enterprise if you have 4+ years of B2B SaaS sales closing experience in Developer/IT/Security technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable closing $30,000–$500,000+ ACV deals and managing complex, multi-stakeholder sales processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a clear written and verbal communicator who can earn trust with both engineers and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a builder mentality and want to help define the go-to-market strategy rather than simply execute an established process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment with significant ownership and limited bureaucracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have sold developer tools, API infrastructure, data infrastructure, cloud platforms, or other technical enterprise products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how APIs are designed, documented, tested, and consumed, and can confidently discuss SDKs, GitHub workflows, CI/CD systems, CLIs, and MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reasonably estimated compensation range for the role is $220,000 to $320,000 OTE, plus a competitive equity package. Actual compensation and leveling is based on the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4036&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What Else?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
